   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Just a comment on a numerical issue​ rather than a biological issue:  The result from pcount is correct as can be seen from a plot of the log likelihood surface:<div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/unmarked/attach/3ff7ff660891b/pcount.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" width=\"360\" height=\"360\"><br>The blue dot is the maximum likelihood estimate.  Using K = 100 gets one an even smaller estimate of the detection probability:  ​0.0323108.  (I also tried K = 150 and obtained the same estimates as with K = 100.)</div><div><br></div><div>Jim<br><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
